      "workedExamples": [
        {
          "exampleId": "EX_GU_JEEMAIN2027_MAT_9BB8FB46_01_POWER_SET_AND_SUBSETS",
          "title": "Power Set and Subsets Listing",
          "problemStatement": "Let $A = \\{1, 2, 3\\}$. Determine:\n(i) The total number of subsets of $A$\n(ii) The number of proper subsets of $A$\n(iii) The explicit power set $P(A)$",
          "stepByStepSolution": [
            "Step 1: Identify the number of elements in set $A$: $n(A) = m = 3$.",
            "Step 2: Calculate the cardinality of the power set using the formula $n(P(A)) = 2^m = 2^3 = 8$.",
            "Step 3: Calculate the number of proper subsets using the formula $2^m - 1 = 2^3 - 1 = 7$.",
            "Step 4: List all subsets systematically by size:\n- Size 0: $\\phi$\n- Size 1: $\\{1\\}, \\{2\\}, \\{3\\}$\n- Size 2: $\\{1, 2\\}, \\{1, 3\\}, \\{2, 3\\}$\n- Size 3: $\\{1, 2, 3\\}$\nThus, $P(A) = \\{\\phi, \\{1\\}, \\{2\\}, \\{3\\}, \\{1, 2\\}, \\{1, 3\\}, \\{2, 3\\}, \\{1, 2, 3\\}\\}$."
          ],
          "finalAnswer": "(i) Total subsets = 8; (ii) Proper subsets = 7; (iii) P(A) = {ϕ, {1}, {2}, {3}, {1,2}, {1,3}, {2,3}, {1,2,3}}",
          "difficulty": "EASY",
          "targetAtomicFactIds": [
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_MAT_9BB8FB46_69C8729D",
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_MAT_9BB8FB46_39AE4B48"
          ],
          "isVerified": true
        },
        {
          "exampleId": "EX_GU_JEEMAIN2027_MAT_9BB8FB46_02_INTERVALS_AND_SET_BUILDER",
          "title": "Real Interval Notation and Classification",
          "problemStatement": "Given the set $S = \\{x \\in \\mathbb{R} : -3 \\le x < 5\\}$:\n(i) Write $S$ in interval notation.\n(ii) Identify whether the endpoints $-3$ and $5$ belong to $S$.\n(iii) Calculate the length of the interval.",
          "stepByStepSolution": [
            "Step 1: Observe the inequalities: $x$ is greater than or equal to $-3$ (inclusive, represented by $[$) and strictly less than $5$ (exclusive, represented by $)$).",
            "Step 2: Express $S$ in interval notation as $[-3, 5)$, which is a semi-open interval.",
            "Step 3: Check endpoint membership: Since $-3 \\le -3 < 5$, $-3 \\in S$. Since $5$ is strictly greater than the upper bound, $5 \\notin S$.",
            "Step 4: Calculate interval length using the formula $b - a = 5 - (-3) = 5 + 3 = 8$."
          ],
          "finalAnswer": "(i) [-3, 5); (ii) -3 ∈ S and 5 ∉ S; (iii) Length = 8",
          "difficulty": "EASY",
          "targetAtomicFactIds": [
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_MAT_9BB8FB46_8E8CCB25",
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_MAT_9BB8FB46_621F66AA",
